id: PHP-SEC-015
ilities: [integrity]
source: cpm
maturity: 2
action: block
title: PHP object injection via unserialize (CVE-2018-15133)
category: security
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .php
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/
  content_contains: unserialize
patterns:
  - regex: unserialize\(.*\$_(GET|POST|REQUEST|COOKIE)
    message: "unserialize() with user input — PHP Object Injection enables RCE via POP chains (CVE-2018-15133)"
  - regex: unserialize\(.*base64_decode
    message: "unserialize() with base64 decoded data — likely processing user-supplied serialized objects"
  - regex: unserialize\(.*file_get_contents
    message: "unserialize() from file — ensure source is trusted, not user-controllable"
fix: Use json_decode() instead. If unserialize is required, use allowed_classes parameter: unserialize($data, ['allowed_classes' => false]).
